IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part8-duties.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART VIII (Offences Against the Person and Reputation):
-- section 214 (definitions for this Part) and sections 215 to 218 (duties tending to preservation of life; abandoning a child).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING). "includes" definitions answer NOTHING for a case they do not list.
-- The party who bears a legal duty is "every one" (s 2 "every one"): the duties below are written for the core `Party` `the accused`, the person in the seat who, if the duty is not performed, may be accused.
-- No time limit is stated for any duty below, so none is invented.

§ `Section 214 -- Interpretation: definitions for Part VIII`

-- src:4399 | abandon or expose includes
-- src:4400 | (a) a wilful omission to take charge of a child by a person who is under a legal duty to do so, and
-- src:4401 | (b) dealing with a child in a manner that is likely to leave that child exposed to risk without protection; (abandonner ou exposer)
@ref s 214 abandon or expose (src:4399-4401)
GIVEN `it is a wilful omission to take charge of a child by a person who is under a legal duty to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is dealing with a child in a manner that is likely to leave that child exposed to risk without protection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214 abandon or expose` MEANS
    IF `it is a wilful omission to take charge of a child by a person who is under a legal duty to do so` OR `it is dealing with a child in a manner that is likely to leave that child exposed to risk without protection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "abandon or expose includes"

-- src:4404 | form of marriage includes a ceremony of marriage that is recognized as valid
-- src:4405 | (a) by the law of the place where it was celebrated, or
-- src:4406 | (b) by the law of the place where an accused is tried, notwithstanding that it is not recognized as valid by the law of the place where it was celebrated; (formalité de mariage)
@ref s 214 form of marriage (src:4404-4406)
GIVEN `it is a ceremony of marriage that is recognized as valid by the law of the place where it was celebrated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a ceremony of marriage that is recognized as valid by the law of the place where an accused is tried, notwithstanding that it is not recognized as valid by the law of the place where it was celebrated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214 form of marriage` MEANS
    IF `it is a ceremony of marriage that is recognized as valid by the law of the place where it was celebrated` OR `it is a ceremony of marriage that is recognized as valid by the law of the place where an accused is tried, notwithstanding that it is not recognized as valid by the law of the place where it was celebrated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "form of marriage includes a ceremony of marriage that is recognized as valid"

-- src:4407 | guardian includes a person who has in law or in fact the custody or control of a child. (tuteur)
@ref s 214 guardian (src:4407-4407)
GIVEN `the person has in law the custody or control of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has in fact the custody or control of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214 guardian` MEANS
    IF `the person has in law the custody or control of a child` OR `the person has in fact the custody or control of a child`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "guardian includes a person who has in law or in fact the custody or control of a child"

§ `Section 215 -- Duty of persons to provide necessaries`

-- src:4414 | (a) as a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family, to provide necessaries of life for a child under the age of sixteen years;
@ref s 215(1)(a) (src:4414-4414)
GIVEN `the person is a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of the child, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1)(a) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` MEANS
    IF `the person is a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family` AND `the age of the child, in years` BELOW 16
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family, to provide necessaries of life for a child under the age of sixteen years" (a scope limit with no "only")

-- src:4415 | (b) to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner; and
@ref s 215(1)(b) (src:4415-4415)
GIVEN `the other person is their spouse, by the ordinary meaning of the word` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is their common-law partner, by s 2 common-law partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1)(b) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner` MEANS
    IF `the other person is their spouse, by the ordinary meaning of the word` OR `the other person is their common-law partner, by s 2 common-law partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner"

-- src:4416 | (c) to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge if that person
-- src:4417 | (i) is unable, by reason of detention, age, illness, mental disorder or other cause, to withdraw himself from that charge, and
-- src:4418 | (ii) is unable to provide himself with necessaries of life.
@ref s 215(1)(c) (src:4416-4418)
GIVEN `the other person is under the person's charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is unable, by reason of detention, age, illness, mental disorder or other cause, to withdraw himself from that charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is unable to provide himself with necessaries of life` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1)(c) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge` MEANS
    IF `the other person is under the person's charge` AND `the other person is unable, by reason of detention, age, illness, mental disorder or other cause, to withdraw himself from that charge` AND `the other person is unable to provide himself with necessaries of life`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge if that person (i) is unable ... to withdraw himself from that charge, and (ii) is unable to provide himself with necessaries of life"

-- src:4413 | 215 (1) Every one is under a legal duty
@ref s 215(1) (src:4413-4413)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) applies, by s 215(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) applies, by s 215(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c) applies, by s 215(1)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1) the person is under a legal duty` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (a) applies, by s 215(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `paragraph (b) applies, by s 215(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `paragraph (c) applies, by s 215(1)(c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one is under a legal duty (a) ... (b) ... (c)" (the text lists three duties without saying there are no others in the Code)

-- src:4413 | 215 (1) Every one is under a legal duty
-- src:4414 | (a) as a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family, to provide necessaries of life for a child under the age of sixteen years;
-- src:4415 | (b) to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner; and
-- src:4416 | (c) to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge if that person
-- src:4417 | (i) is unable, by reason of detention, age, illness, mental disorder or other cause, to withdraw himself from that charge, and
-- src:4418 | (ii) is unable to provide himself with necessaries of life.
@ref s 215(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4413-4418)
DECLARE `s 215(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(1)(a) provide necessaries of life for the child`
    `s 215(1)(b) provide necessaries of life to the spouse or common-law partner`
    `s 215(1)(c) provide necessaries of life to the person under the person's charge`

@ref s 215(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4413-4418)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215(1) act`
`s 215(1)(a) the duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 215(1)(a) provide necessaries of life for the child`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 215(1)(a): the necessaries of life were not provided for the child"

@ref s 215(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4413-4418)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215(1) act`
`s 215(1)(b) the duty to provide necessaries of life to the spouse or common-law partner` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 215(1)(b) provide necessaries of life to the spouse or common-law partner`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 215(1)(b): the necessaries of life were not provided to the spouse or common-law partner"

@ref s 215(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4413-4418)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215(1) act`
`s 215(1)(c) the duty to provide necessaries of life to the person under the person's charge` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 215(1)(c) provide necessaries of life to the person under the person's charge`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 215(1)(c): the necessaries of life were not provided to the person under the person's charge"

-- src:4420 | (2) Every person commits an offence who, being under a legal duty within the meaning of subsection (1), fails without lawful excuse to perform that duty, if
-- src:4421 | (a) with respect to a duty imposed by paragraph (1)(a) or (b),
-- src:4422 | (i) the person to whom the duty is owed is in destitute or necessitous circumstances, or
-- src:4423 | (ii) the failure to perform the duty endangers the life of the person to whom the duty is owed, or causes or is likely to cause the health of that person to be endangered permanently; or
-- src:4424 | (b) with respect to a duty imposed by paragraph (1)(c), the failure to perform the duty endangers the life of the person to whom the duty is owed or causes or is likely to cause the health of that person to be injured permanently.
@ref s 215(2) (src:4420-4424)
GIVEN `the person is under a legal duty, by s 215(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the duty is imposed by paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duty is imposed by paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to whom the duty is owed is in destitute or necessitous circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure endangers the life of the person to whom the duty is owed, or causes or is likely to cause the health of that person to be endangered permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure endangers the life of the person to whom the duty is owed or causes or is likely to cause the health of that person to be injured permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is under a legal duty, by s 215(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person fails to perform the duty` AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`)
           AND (   (`the duty is imposed by paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` AND (`the person to whom the duty is owed is in destitute or necessitous circumstances` OR `the failure endangers the life of the person to whom the duty is owed, or causes or is likely to cause the health of that person to be endangered permanently`))
                OR (`the duty is imposed by paragraph (1)(c)` AND `the failure endangers the life of the person to whom the duty is owed or causes or is likely to cause the health of that person to be injured permanently`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is under a legal duty, by s 215(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person fails to perform the duty` AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "fails without lawful excuse to perform that duty, if (a) ... or (b) ..." (the offence arises only if the paragraph (a) or (b) condition is met: marginal reading M2)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who, being under a legal duty within the meaning of subsection (1), fails without lawful excuse to perform that duty"

-- src:4426 | (3) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (2)
-- src:4427 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:4428 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 215(3) (src:4426-4428)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 215(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4427 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
@ref s 215(3)(a) (src:4427-4427)
`s 215(3)(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4426 | (3) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (2)
-- src:4427 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:4428 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 215(3) (src:4426-4428)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 215(3) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 215(3)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4432 | (b) evidence that a person has in any way recognized a child as being his child is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the child is his child;
@ref s 215(4)(b) (src:4432-4432)
GIVEN `the person has in any way recognized a child as being his child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(4)(b) the recognition is proof that the child is his child` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has in any way recognized a child as being his child` AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person has in any way recognized a child as being his child` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the child is his child" (marginal reading M2)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence that a person has in any way recognized a child as being his child"

-- src:4433 | (c) evidence that a person has failed for a period of one month to make provision for the maintenance of any child of theirs under the age of sixteen years is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the person has failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child; and
@ref s 215(4)(c) (src:4433-4433)
-- Fork F6: "a period of one month" is complete on the corresponding day of the next month (`add months`); the other reading counts it complete a day later.
GIVEN `the date from which the person failed to make provision for the maintenance of the child` IS A DATE
      `the date as at which the failure is assessed` IS A DATE
      `the child is a child of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of the child, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the child is a child of the person`) OR `the age of the child, in years` AT LEAST 16
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any child of theirs under the age of sixteen years"
        IF `the date as at which the failure is assessed` BELOW `add months` `the date from which the person failed to make provision for the maintenance of the child` 1
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has failed for a period of one month" (a period the text fixes in its own words)
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof" (marginal reading M2)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:4434 | (d) the fact that a spouse or common-law partner or child is receiving or has received necessaries of life from another person who is not under a legal duty to provide them is not a defence.
@ref s 215(4)(d) (src:4434-4434)
GIVEN `the spouse, common-law partner or child is receiving or has received necessaries of life from another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that other person is not under a legal duty to provide them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(4)(d) the receipt of necessaries of life from another person is a defence` MEANS
    IF `the spouse, common-law partner or child is receiving or has received necessaries of life from another person` AND `that other person is not under a legal duty to provide them`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the fact that a spouse or common-law partner or child is receiving or has received necessaries of life from another person who is not under a legal duty to provide them is not a defence"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not a defence" is said only of receipt from a person not under a legal duty

§ `Sections 216 to 218`

-- src:4436 | 216 Every one who undertakes to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person or to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person is, except in cases of necessity, under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care in so doing.
@ref s 216 (src:4436-4436)
GIVEN `the person undertakes to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person undertakes to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a case of necessity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216 the person is under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person undertakes to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person` OR `the person undertakes to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person`) AND `it is a case of necessity`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in cases of necessity"
        IF `the person undertakes to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person` OR `the person undertakes to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who undertakes to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person or to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person"

@ref s 216 (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4436-4436)
DECLARE `s 216 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 216 have and use reasonable knowledge, skill and care in the treatment or act undertaken`

@ref s 216 (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4436-4436)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 216 act`
`s 216 the duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 216 have and use reasonable knowledge, skill and care in the treatment or act undertaken`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 216: reasonable knowledge, skill and care were not had and used"

-- src:4438 | 217 Every one who undertakes to do an act is under a legal duty to do it if an omission to do the act is or may be dangerous to life.
@ref s 217 (src:4438-4438)
GIVEN `the person undertakes to do an act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an omission to do the act is or may be dangerous to life` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 217 the person is under a legal duty to do the act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person undertakes to do an act` AND `an omission to do the act is or may be dangerous to life` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person undertakes to do an act` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is under a legal duty to do it if an omission to do the act is or may be dangerous to life" (marginal reading M2)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who undertakes to do an act"

@ref s 217 (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4438-4438)
DECLARE `s 217 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 217 do the act undertaken`

@ref s 217 (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4438-4438)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 217 act`
`s 217 the duty to do the act undertaken` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 217 do the act undertaken`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 217: the act undertaken was not done"

-- src:4440 | 217.1 Every one who undertakes, or has the authority, to direct how another person does work or performs a task is under a legal duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm to that person, or any other person, arising from that work or task.
@ref s 217.1 (src:4440-4440)
GIVEN `the person undertakes, or has the authority, to direct how another person does work or performs a task` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 217.1 the person is under a legal duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm` MEANS
    IF `the person undertakes, or has the authority, to direct how another person does work or performs a task`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who undertakes, or has the authority, to direct how another person does work or performs a task"

@ref s 217.1 (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4440-4440)
DECLARE `s 217.1 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 217.1 take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm arising from the work or task`

@ref s 217.1 (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4440-4440)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 217.1 act`
`s 217.1 the duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 217.1 take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm arising from the work or task`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 217.1: reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm arising from the work or task were not taken"

-- src:4442 | 218 Every one who unlawfully abandons or exposes a child who is under the age of ten years, so that its life is or is likely to be endangered or its health is or is likely to be permanently injured,
-- src:4443 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:4444 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 218 (src:4442-4444)
GIVEN `the person unlawfully abandons or exposes a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of the child, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the child's life is or is likely to be endangered or its health is or is likely to be permanently injured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218 the person commits the offence of abandoning a child` MEANS
    IF `the person unlawfully abandons or exposes a child` AND `the age of the child, in years` BELOW 10 AND `the child's life is or is likely to be endangered or its health is or is likely to be permanently injured`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who unlawfully abandons or exposes a child who is under the age of ten years, so that its life is or is likely to be endangered or its health is or is likely to be permanently injured, (a) is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 218 (src:4442-4444)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 218 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 218(a) (src:4443-4443)
`s 218(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 218 (src:4442-4444)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 218 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 218(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
